  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable pastoral systems and their Youth, Burkina Faso and Mauritania: Updates and actions for a social contract</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Updated understanding and data: The conditions of sustainable pastoral household economy are analysed in relation to the migration of young people and their trajectories of emancipation. Endogenous protection mechanisms, access to external services of social protection, the use of public services, and the avenues for the extension of a social policy adapted to pastoralist populations are characterized. The situations of displaced young people are analysed in relation to structural social changes in the pastoral household economy, allowing to identify avenues for public action with a view on long-term change. 
Capacity building through collaborative survey: The involvement of POs/CSOs in this research action facilitates their collective and cross-reflection on the status of youth and pastoral dynamics, hence the empowerment of their reflection and its anchoring in the social changes
Formulation of a project document tentatively titled ?Pastoralism and its youth in the Sahel in 2020: which social contract for which future??</narrative>
  </description>
